│ patch_description        │ Replace the clipped concentric-ring construction with a deterministic constrained         │
│                          │ nonlinear packing search. The old outer ring placed many centers on the boundary after    │
│                          │ clipping, forcing extremely small radii. The new constructor starts from a dense 5-by-5   │
│                          │ square packing plus a small corner circle, then uses SLSQP with analytic derivatives to   │
│                          │ move all centers and vary every radius simultaneously.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The optimization directly maximizes the sum of radii subject to four boundary             │
│                          │ inequalities per circle and a squared-distance non-overlap inequality for every pair. A   │
│                          │ second staggered layered seed is also tested, since hexagonal-like rows can escape the    │
│                          │ square-grid local optimum. Finally, a uniform feasibility repair scale protects against   │
│                          │ tiny numerical constraint violations while preserving the optimized shape. If SciPy is    │
│                          │ unavailable, the already-valid dense seed is returned.                                    │
