│ patch_description        │ Expand the staggered-start portfolio with structurally distinct five-row topologies,      │
│                          │ especially arrangements having adjacent six-circle rows.  The best 26-circle packings are │
│                          │ sensitive to which layers carry the extra circles: moving a six-circle row changes the    │
│                          │ boundary contact graph and permits different unequal-radius defects near corners.  These  │
│                          │ seeds remain feasible at the existing radius 0.075, so the solver begins from valid dense │
│                          │ configurations.  This is a targeted diversification of contact graphs rather than random  │
│                          │ perturbations, retaining the fast analytic constraint Jacobian and selecting the best     │
│                          │ feasible result.                                                                          │
