│ patch_name               │ staged_multistart_refinement                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Use a continuation strategy before the fully unequal-radius solve.  The early stages      │
│                          │ impose a modest common lower bound on every radius, preventing SLSQP from immediately     │
│                          │ creating tiny sacrificial circles while it determines a well-spread contact graph.        │
│                          │ Subsequent stages relax that floor and allow the unequal boundary/interior radii needed   │
│                          │ for the best total.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Also add several reproducible lattice perturbations.  Different small perturbations lead  │
│                          │ to different active-contact graphs, which is particularly important near the current 2.62 │
│                          │ local optimum.  The final unrestricted stage retains the best result from every           │
│                          │ trajectory, so the added exploration cannot discard a stronger candidate found in an      │
│                          │ earlier run.                                                                              │
