│ patch_description        │ This constructor replaces the ring heuristic with a topology-guided nonlinear packing     │
│                          │ search. It starts from several asymmetric five-row layouts, especially layouts containing │
│                          │ one or two denser six-circle rows, because these exploit the square boundary more         │
│                          │ effectively than a fully symmetric grid.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ For each candidate row topology, the program jointly optimizes all circle centers and     │
│                          │ radii using constrained SLSQP optimization. The objective is the total radius, while      │
│                          │ constraints enforce square containment and every pairwise non-overlap condition. A final  │
│                          │ certification pass uniformly shrinks radii only if required by floating-point tolerance,  │
│                          │ ensuring the returned packing is valid.                                                   │
