│ patch_description        │ Retain the strongest distinct first-pass solutions and re-optimize them from a            │
│                          │ microscopically deflated feasible state using substantially tighter tolerances. Different │
│                          │ perturbations can converge to different contact graphs with nearly equal initial scores;  │
│                          │ a graph that is marginally worse after the broad pass can improve beyond the incumbent    │
│                          │ when its tangencies are settled accurately. Deflating radii before refinement avoids      │
│                          │ retaining tiny SLSQP constraint violations and lets the optimizer re-establish the active │
│                          │ boundary and circle contacts cleanly.                                                     │
