│ patch_name               │ seed_geometry_variants                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Add deterministic geometric variants to every row-layout seed before nonlinear            │
│                          │ optimization.  The existing random jitter breaks some symmetry, but the row patterns      │
│                          │ still tend to enter a small number of contact graphs.  Reflecting the indexed             │
│                          │ configuration can lead SLSQP through a different active-set trajectory, while a small     │
│                          │ alternating row displacement more directly encourages triangular-lattice contacts and     │
│                          │ asymmetric boundary defects.  The displacement is far smaller than the initial clearance  │
│                          │ implied by the low starting radii, so every generated seed remains safely feasible.  This │
│                          │ increases basin coverage without changing the public interface or the final feasibility   │
│                          │ certification.                                                                            │
