│ patch_description        │ Seed the nonlinear solver with deterministic unequal radii correlated with the finite-row │
│                          │ topology.  Corner-adjacent circles receive a modest radius advantage, while circles in    │
│                          │ the densest six-circle rows receive a slight penalty.  This breaks the artificial         │
│                          │ equal-radius basin before contacts are established and better reflects the boundary       │
│                          │ defects expected in strong finite square packings.  The radii remain deliberately small   │
│                          │ relative to initial separations, so all starts are feasible without requiring an          │
│                          │ unreliable repair before optimization.                                                    │
