│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ unequal_hex_continuation                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The prior constructor used five layered layouts, a common-radius continuation stage       │
│                          │ (`maxiter=550`), and equal-radius or low-radius final starts (`maxiter=1450`), followed   │
│                          │ by a long polish. This revision preserves that effective staged SLSQP structure but adds  │
│                          │ topology-aware unequal-radius starts after the common-radius stage. Each common-radius    │
│                          │ packing is converted into several strictly feasible heterogeneous radius vectors: circles │
│                          │ with more interior clearance are initially larger, while boundary and alternating-layer   │
│                          │ circles are slightly smaller. The perturbation amplitude is deliberately limited (`8%`)   │
│                          │ and globally buffered (`0.90*q`) so starts remain feasible without relying on solver      │
│                          │ recovery. This helps SLSQP enter asymmetric unequal-radius contact graphs directly rather │
│                          │ than first converging through a rigid symmetric basin. The search also uses deterministic │
│                          │ mirrored/phase-shifted profiles, refined common-stage tolerance, and a final              │
│                          │ high-accuracy polish of the best basin.                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
