│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lp_contact_search                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This constructor replaces purely radius-uniform starts with a two-level approach. Each    │
│                          │ layered, asymmetric topology first receives radii from a fixed-center linear program:     │
│                          │ wall limits and every pairwise separation become linear radius constraints once centers   │
│                          │ are fixed. This produces unequal boundary-aware radii before nonlinear optimization       │
│                          │ begins.                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The nonlinear stage then performs simultaneous center/radius contact optimization from a  │
│                          │ portfolio of twelve asymmetric hexagonal-row seeds, including the recommended five-row    │
│                          │ layouts and their vertical reversals. Unlike the previous equal-radius continuation, the  │
│                          │ LP initialization deliberately introduces useful radius asymmetry early, allowing SLSQP   │
│                          │ to explore contact graphs with small sacrificial boundary circles and larger interior     │
│                          │ circles. Candidates are conservatively normalized before comparison and again before      │
│                          │ return, ensuring strict validity.                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0786                                                                                   │
