│ patch_description        │ Replace repeated perturbations of one row topology with a fixed portfolio of twelve       │
│                          │ geometrically distinct staggered layouts.  Unequal five-row population patterns alter the │
│                          │ boundary contact graph before nonlinear refinement begins; this is more valuable than     │
│                          │ spending most starts on small random changes to the same basin.  In particular, placing   │
│                          │ the two six-circle rows asymmetrically gives interior circles triangular support while    │
│                          │ allowing different top and bottom boundary layers.  Both orientations are retained        │
│                          │ because the square is symmetric geometrically but SLSQP follows coordinate-dependent      │
│                          │ local trajectories and can refine transposed contact graphs differently.                  │
